---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const trail = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Contact', href: '/contact/' }];
---
<Page
  title="Contact Going Eagle"
  eyebrow="Get in touch"
  description="How to reach Going Eagle with a correction, a question about a recommendation, or a partnership enquiry."
  intro="Corrections are the most useful thing you can send us. If something on this site is wrong, we want to fix it."
  trail={trail}
>
  <h2>Corrections and factual queries</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us the page and what is wrong with it. Reader corrections have changed recommendations
    on this site before. We would rather be corrected than consistent.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions about a recommendation</h2>
  <p>
    If you are trying to decide between two products and our page did not settle it, send us the
    specifics — your handicap, your typical miss, and your budget. That context usually changes
    the answer, and it tells us where a guide needs improving.
  </p>

  <h2>Brands and partnerships</h2>
  <p>
    We do not accept payment for reviews, placements or rankings, so please do not ask. We are
    happy to hear from brands who want a product considered on the same terms as everything else
    on the site — read <a href="/gear/how-we-test/">how we test</a> first so expectations are
    clear.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p class="callout-title">Contact details</p>
    <p>
      An email address and contact form will be published here once the site's mailbox is
      configured. We are not publishing a placeholder address that bounces.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
